    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's mixed, but you said it wasn't \"designed\" to be a win for workers. so if we're looking at the actual outcomes, isn't it basically a fact that it ended up being a failure for the working class? like, if the net result was more job losses in manufacturing and stagnant wages, isn't that a clear-cut failure regardless of what the \"intent\" was?",
