      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While you are correct that significant job losses in manufacturing occurred, claiming the TPP was an outright \"failure\" is complex because some studies also point to modest long-term gains in productivity and wage growth in other sectors. The agreement primarily succeeded in expanding U.S. exports and corporate investment, which supports economic arguments for trade, even if it failed to protect specific de-industrialized communities. In political science terms, it is often viewed as a partial conflict success for international capital rather than a total societal failure, depending heavily on how one weighs aggregate economic metrics against localized community impacts.",
